course: dictionary
lesson: 51
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accuracy means being correct and exact, with no mistakes. «A correction is a notice fixing a mistake in a news story; admitting mistakes shows a news source cares about accuracy.» The news source cares about getting its facts right, so accuracy here means being correct.
explain: Accuracy has a second meaning: the skill of hitting or reaching exactly what you aim at. A player who keeps the ball in the net has good accuracy. Both meanings are about being exact, but one is about facts and the other is about aim.
explain: Look at the words around accuracy. Words like check, measure, mistake and correct point to the first meaning. Words like shoot, aim and hit point to the second. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accuracy is a noun that you cannot count, so you say "more accuracy", not "three accuracies".
fact: «Accuracy» means being correct and exact, with no mistakes.
fact: «Accuracy» can also mean the skill of hitting or reaching exactly what you aim at, as in shooting.
fact: In maths and science, you can measure with accuracy, or give an answer to a set degree of accuracy, such as one decimal place.
fact: Useful phrases: "check for accuracy" means look carefully for mistakes, and "to the nearest" means rounded to a given size, such as the nearest whole number.
exercise: «A correction is a notice fixing a mistake in a news story; admitting mistakes shows a news source cares about accuracy.» What does accuracy mean here? | *Being correct and exact, with no mistakes | Being old and worn | Being very fast | Being shiny and new
exercise: Maya says, «Her shooting accuracy was brilliant; the ball went straight into the basket every time.» What does accuracy mean here? | Being correct about her facts | *The skill of hitting exactly what she aims at | Being tired after the game | Being quiet and calm
exercise: Which phrase means looking carefully for mistakes? | Full of colour | With a loud voice | To the nearest | *Check for accuracy
test: Sam measured the table «with great accuracy» so the wood fitted perfectly. What does accuracy mean here? | Being happy about the table | Being loud and easy to hear | The skill of throwing a ball far | *Being correct and exact, with no mistakes
test: Which sentence uses accuracy in the sense of hitting a target? | *The archer's accuracy won her the gold medal | The newspaper printed a correction for its accuracy | The answer was rounded to the nearest whole number | Our teacher asked us to check for accuracy
exam: Which word means the same as accuracy when it means being correct and exact? | Speed | *Exactness | Loudness | Colour
